00:45:38.000 --> 00:46:13.000
Jason Rinker feels the same, but he says the ordeal has left him with some insight into dying. I think the mistake is in thinking that we know how we're going to react to everything. You know, if I were to ask you, at the end of your life, would you like to suffer for two and a half years or would you prefer to go out peacefully on your own terms in hospice? I can't imagine anyone saying, well, I would take the suffering. But when you're in that moment, and I've thought about this so many times, she wasn't necessarily thinking rationally. She was thinking about, well, tomorrow,

